WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:02.445
"Hey, Patrick!"

2
00:00:02.446 --> 00:00:09.458
"Hey, Dell." Patrick turned and grinned at Dell, one of the pitchers on the Central Middle School baseball team.

3
00:00:09.459 --> 00:00:17.528
Dell was long, with long arms and long legs. Even his face was long below long brown hair, which he wore tied back.

4
00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:23.929
Dell was an eighth-grader this year, a year older than Patrick, and he was sure to be a starter for the baseball team.

5
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:29.604
Dell held up a baseball, and Patrick instantly went into his catcher's stance.

6
00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:33.771
He tucked his free hand safely behind him and lifted his mitt.

7
00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:38.255
Dell buzzed the baseball straight across the empty parking lot.

8
00:00:38.256 --> 00:00:44.172
Smack! Patrick loved the sound of the ball hitting the mitt's sweet spot.

9
00:00:44.173 --> 00:00:50.330
"You ready to play ball?" called Dell as Patrick slung the ball back.

10
00:00:50.331 --> 00:00:55.198
"I sure am!" said Patrick. "Have you been working on your changeup?"

11
00:00:55.199 --> 00:01:00.321
A changeup was a slow pitch, but it was thrown just like a fast one to trick the batter.

12
00:01:00.322 --> 00:01:02.510
Dell nodded. "Yep."

13
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:08.395
"Let me see it." Patrick signaled the pitch by wiggling four fingers between his legs.

14
00:01:08.396 --> 00:01:13.077
Dell pulled his arm back and let the ball fly.

15
00:01:13.078 --> 00:01:17.238
It zipped toward the mitt and then seemed to float as it got nearer.

16
00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:26.390
Smack! Patrick caught it. "That was perfect!" He stood and lobbed the ball back to Dell.

17
00:01:26.391 --> 00:01:32.305
By now the parking lot was full of Dragons players.

18
00:01:32.306 --> 00:01:38.128
Patrick waved at familiar faces as Dell trotted over to walk onto the baseball field with him.

19
00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:42.474
Energy ripped through Patrick like a vibrating guitar string.

20
00:01:42.475 --> 00:01:46.058
"Man, this is going to be a great year!" he thought.

21
00:01:46.059 --> 00:01:55.131
It was a warm, sunny Saturday—the very first day of baseball practice. Although it was still February, it felt like spring outside.

22
00:01:55.132 --> 00:02:03.896
Patrick dumped his equipment on the bench in the dugout and reached for the old catcher's mitt his brother, Daniel, had given him on the drive over to the middle school.

23
00:02:03.897 --> 00:02:08.544
The mitt's leather was soft and supple like a comfortable old shoe.

24
00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:14.859
"You should use your own mitt every day," Daniel had said. "But keep this one for luck."

25
00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.391
Patrick hoped he wouldn't need luck.

26
00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:23.519
He was in seventh grade now and ready to leave Little League behind and play middle school baseball.

27
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.087
He was ready to be a Central Middle School Dragon.

28
00:02:27.088 --> 00:02:33.592
A stocky kid with curly black hair hopped out of a red pickup.

29
00:02:33.593 --> 00:02:41.259
He looked around uncertainly for a second and then hauled a canvas bag out of the back of the truck.

30
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.604
Patrick nudged Dell. "Who's the new kid?"

31
00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:47.663
Dell shrugged. "Haven't seen him before."

32
00:02:47.664 --> 00:02:54.582
"He just moved into my neighborhood," said Todd, a big and bulky pinch hitter who also played left field.

33
00:02:54.583 --> 00:03:00.160
"You'll see him at school on Monday. He's in eighth grade. Seems like a nice guy."

34
00:03:00.161 --> 00:03:04.069
Dell grinned. "Yeah, but can he play?"

35
00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:08.987
Todd shrugged. "Coach let him join the team. He must be pretty good."

36
00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:15.304
"I hope so," said Patrick. He wanted the team to make it to the championship this year.

37
00:03:15.305 --> 00:03:19.563
"Practice starts in three minutes, boys!" barked Coach.

38
00:03:19.564 --> 00:03:25.036
Patrick buckled on his shin guards and chest protector and then picked up his mask.

39
00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:29.584
Daniel, who was volunteering as an assistant coach, was already at home plate.

40
00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:33.870
Patrick wasn't sure whether having his brother here was good or bad.

41
00:03:33.871 --> 00:03:39.614
The good thing was that Daniel was a great ballplayer. The bad thing was—

42
00:03:39.615 --> 00:03:46.932
"Yo, Daniel!" Just then Dell raced for the mound, waving enthusiastically at Daniel.

43
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:50.461
"It's awesome that you're going to be coaching!"

44
00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:54.516
The bad thing was that everyone still remembered Daniel Deboe.

45
00:03:54.517 --> 00:03:58.788
The Dragons had won the championship both years that Daniel caught for the team.

46
00:03:58.789 --> 00:04:02.764
Now he was in high school, but he had become a living legend.

47
00:04:02.765 --> 00:04:06.525
"Warm up, guys," yelled Daniel, smacking his gum.

48
00:04:06.526 --> 00:04:11.948
As he strutted toward Coach, he grinned at Patrick.

49
00:04:11.949 --> 00:04:14.914
"Maybe I'll put in a good word for you as starter."

50
00:04:14.915 --> 00:04:20.676
Patrick straightened his shoulders and grinned back. "Don't need praise when you got plays!"

51
00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:25.990
"That's right, little bro. Don't worry, you'll fit right into the team."

52
00:04:25.991 --> 00:04:33.164
Patrick wasn't really worried about belonging on the team. He already knew a lot of the other kids from playing Little League.

53
00:04:33.165 --> 00:04:36.899
Plus, because of Daniel, he knew some older players too.

54
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.816
The only hard part of playing a middle school sport was keeping up with his classwork.

55
00:04:41.817 --> 00:04:45.666
He'd struggled with math since the beginning of the year.

56
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:51.464
Daniel pushed the front of his hair back; a similar thick blond curl hung on Patrick's forehead.

57
00:04:51.465 --> 00:04:58.281
"Just don't get your hopes up," Daniel went on. "Coach hardly ever starts seventh- graders at the beginning of the season."

58
00:04:58.282 --> 00:05:02.289
"You made starter for the first game," Patrick pointed out.

59
00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.114
Daniel shrugged.

60
00:05:04.115 --> 00:05:12.293
Patrick knew that shrug. It meant, "But I'm really good." Which might have been bragging, but it was true.

61
00:05:12.294 --> 00:05:18.290
Daniel had short, heavy legs that rested naturally in the catcher's crouch. Good balance.

62
00:05:18.291 --> 00:05:25.580
A long reach and a quick, hard throw. And he read the game of baseball like a champion chess player read the chessboard.

63
00:05:25.581 --> 00:05:28.540
Daniel was built to be a catcher.

64
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:35.364
"I don't want to play in Daniel's shadow," Patrick thought as he watched Daniel consulting with Coach about a few things.

65
00:05:35.365 --> 00:05:41.188
Patrick was shorter and lighter than his brother but just as quick. And he worked hard.

66
00:05:41.189 --> 00:05:48.927
He slipped his hand in his mitt and flexed his fingers. This was the year to make his own mark on Dragons baseball history.

67
00:05:48.928 --> 00:05:52.334
It was his turn to catch for the team.

68
00:05:52.335 --> 00:05:57.452
The new kid from the red truck dumped his bag next to Patrick's.

69
00:05:57.453 --> 00:05:59.499
"Hey. I'm Patrick."

70
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:06.070
"Mickey. My family just moved here. Patrick Deboe, right? I've heard you're pretty good."

71
00:06:06.071 --> 00:06:09.902
Patrick shrugged. "I've been playing awhile."

72
00:06:09.903 --> 00:06:14.684
"Me too." Mickey grinned. "Started playing T-ball and kept going.

73
00:06:14.685 --> 00:06:20.976
I was hoping to make starter at my old school, but my mom got transferred here before baseball season began."

74
00:06:20.977 --> 00:06:24.377
"That's tough," said Patrick.

75
00:06:24.378 --> 00:06:31.217
Mickey shrugged. "Nothing I can do about it. I'm lucky that Coach is letting me on the team since I missed tryouts."

76
00:06:31.218 --> 00:06:36.381
"Coach does what's best for the team. So you must be a good player," said Patrick.

77
00:06:36.382 --> 00:06:42.047
"I hope I don't disappoint him." Mickey reached into his bag.

78
00:06:42.048 --> 00:06:49.086
Patrick was about to ask what position Mickey played. Then he saw what Mickey had pulled out.

79
00:06:49.087 --> 00:06:56.323
A catcher's mitt.

